# O. DISCLOSURE AND PRESENTATION

## PM-DISC-001 — DisclosureContext

Binds principal, login session, client instance, Host, scope, policy, Auth epoch, expiry/lease.

## PM-DISC-002 — DisclosureContext Lifecycle

Issued/active/expired/revoked/invalidated semantics are explicit. Terminal context never reopens.

## PM-DISC-003 — Revocation Propagation Bound

Protected streaming has a bounded revocation-propagation guarantee or uses short self-expiring leases. If neither can be guaranteed, the protected stream is unavailable.

## PM-DISC-004 — Stale Read-Only

Core/source loss does not extend grants. Sensitive data purges at enforceable expiry; permitted non-sensitive cache may remain visibly stale.

## PM-DISC-005 — Non-Disclosing Existence

Where existence is protected, client distinctions may collapse across `NOT_FOUND`, `DENIED`, ActionAvailability, history/evidence lookup, counts, and related paths.

## PM-CLASS-001 — Disclosure Classification

Each protected class defines eligible presentation paths, persistence, swap/hibernate/crash rules, externalization, mandatory audit, retention/disposal, and declassification behavior.

## PM-CLASS-002 — Presentation Classes

Examples: `ORDINARY_MANAGER_UI`, `TRUSTED_PRIME_PRESENTATION_PATH`, `BROKER_ONLY`, `NOT_PRESENTABLE`.

## PM-CLASS-003 — Capability-Based Presentation

A class may use a presentation path only if that path can enforce the required egress/capture/persistence/accessibility controls. No best-effort security claim.

## PM-CLASS-004 — Classification Propagation

Derived data inherits relevant sensitivity unless a versioned authoritative declassification/coarsening transform explicitly changes it.

## PM-CLASS-005 — Digest Classification

Hashes/digests are not automatically declassified.

## PM-CLASS-006 — Logical Revocation Is Not Forensic Erasure

Projection purge stops authorized access; it does not promise forensic zeroization of webview heap, swap, hibernation, or prior external copies. Classes requiring stronger post-display erasure must not enter ordinary renderer memory.

## PM-DISC-006 — Positive Disclosure Release Law

Protected bytes leave Prime authority only when the DisclosureContext is current, classification is known, presentation/egress path is eligible, query/filter/sort semantics are authorized, mandatory audit is accepted, authorized transforms are applied, and no mandatory disclosure UNKNOWN remains.

## PM-PORTAL-001 — Scoped Externalization Capability

If protected clipboard/save/print/download/navigation is offered, it must use an authoritative scoped Prime portal/capability. Manager does not gain broad filesystem/home/network authority merely for convenience.

## PM-COMPLETE-001 — Async Completion Authorization

Action completion UI/notifications are authorized at delivery time. Session B does not inherit Session A’s completion disclosure merely because it is now active.

