# Q. CONTROL REQUESTS, PREFLIGHT, AND PRIVILEGED ADMISSION

## PM-REQUEST-001 — Control Request Result

Pre-admission results such as `DENIED`, `PROHIBITED`, `STALE`, `UNSUPPORTED`, `INCOMPATIBLE`, `REQUIRES_STEP_UP`, `PREFLIGHT_REQUIRED`, and `INVALID_REQUEST` are not Host Actions and guarantee `NO_MACHINE_EFFECT` for the rejected request.

## PM-PREFLIGHT-001 — Preflight Purity

Preflight does not hide the target effect.

## PM-OBS-001 — ObservationCostDescriptor

Observation capabilities declare passive, activation-required, or invasive behavior, resource-cost class, expected side effects, Provider/device/runtime activation requirement, and whether explicit authorization/evidence is required.

## PM-PREFLIGHT-002 — Explicit Observation Activation

If deeper inspection requires activation, that activation is an explicit separately governed/evidenced effect; after state settles, preflight reruns.

## PM-PREFLIGHT-003 — PreflightReceipt

Binds canonical request digest, target/set identity, relevant revisions/fences, Provider/incarnation, placement, DependencyGraph revision, control-session/control-path revisions, Impact/Protection/Risk assessment references, closure state, observation activations already completed, expiry, and disclosure-safe approval projection.

## PM-PREFLIGHT-004 — Receipt Lifecycle

Issued/active/expired/consumed/invalidated semantics are explicit. Terminal receipt never reopens.

## PM-REQ-001 — Candidate Effect Identity

Candidate effect ID exists before trusted approval.

## PM-REQ-002 — Approval Binding

Trusted approval binds candidate ID + request digest + preflight receipt + assurance context.

## PM-REQ-003 — Final Re-Evaluation

Core recomputes current safety/authorization at the admission boundary.

## PM-REQ-004 — Crash-Consistent Redemption

Authorization is durably bound to exactly one candidate ID. Same authorization + different candidate ID is denied.

## PM-REQ-005 — Definitive Rejection Tombstone

Definitively rejected candidate cannot later become admitted. Rejection/replay tombstone persists across any restart that could outlive the retry/approval horizon.

## PM-REQ-006 — Redeemed Not Admitted

After crash, the same candidate may be explicitly reconciled/resumed only after fresh revalidation and while the approval remains applicable. It never silently auto-resubmits.

## PM-REQ-007 — Request Namespace Binding

Candidate/request replay namespaces bind Host identity, Security-State version, and requesting client/system authority.

## PM-REQ-008 — No Hidden Local Mutation Queue

Core disconnect before admission never causes the broker to silently queue and auto-submit later. Reconcile the candidate first; if not admitted, require the contract-defined explicit resume/fresh path.

